{
  "_README": "Hand-labeled golden set for extraction CORRECTNESS (not similarity to a model). One record per job in gemini-sample-jobs.json, labeled from exactly what the extractor sees (first 6000 chars of description_text) and graded against the production prompt's own rules (e.g. Jira/Slack/Excel are excluded from tech_stack). `expected` is the best answer; `acceptable` lists defensible alternatives for genuinely ambiguous fields. tech_required entries must appear (an array entry = synonyms, any one counts); tech_allowed entries are borderline items that are not penalized; anything else in a model's tech_stack counts against precision. Scored by scoreAgainstGolden() in web/lib/ai/eval/agreement.ts. Labeled 2026-11-15 by Claude Code; spot-check before treating as gospel.",
